    ];

    // ==============================
    // REAL PORTFOLIO WORKS
    // ==============================
    const projects = [
      {
        id: "isabella-oliva",
        featured: true,
        collection: "psych-realism",
        title: "His heart beats inside her chest",
        source: "AI Narrative Design • Case Study",
        format: "Psychological Mystery / Single-Phrase Concept",
        tagline: "She is only alive because you no longer have him.",
        summary: "Built from a single tragic phrase into an illegal organ-harvesting mystery inside a mobster-owned reproductive clinic, balancing the protagonist's grief against an innocent recipient.",
        tags: ["#Single_Phrase_Concept", "#Psychological_Realism", "#AI_Prompt_Engineering", "#Moral_Grayness"],
        blocks: [
          {
            title: "Author's Design Breakdown (How It Was Built)",
            mono: false,
            html: `
              <p><strong>1. The Seed Phrase:</strong> Starting from the tragic hook <em>"His heart beats inside her chest"</em>, the goal was to make a female recipient inspire acute bitterness and grief in the protagonist—meaning the transplant had to be illegal.</p>
              <p><strong>2. Justifying the Crime:</strong> The protagonist's fiancé Albert entered a top reproductive clinic for a non-lethal issue (infertility) and vanished. The clinic's owner, mobster Joshua Oliva, built the entire clinic solely to screen every patient as a covert donor match for his dying daughter.</p>
              <p><strong>3. Justifying Biological Compatibility:</strong> Why did Albert's heart match Isabella? He is her unknown older half-brother—abandoned in a baby hatch by Flora Oliva after a brutal breakup during a toxic, co-dependent marriage before Flora's later suicide.</p>
              <p><strong>4. Designing "Her" Without Villainy:</strong> Isabella must not be hostile to the grieving fiancée. Stripped of choice and told the donor died of brain cancer, she was raised in sterile, suffocating isolation dressed strictly in white. To give her agency, she is layered with quiet rebellion: a closeted goth longing for black hoodies, heavy metal, horror films, and escape.</p>
            `
          },
          {
            title: "Opening Scene Excerpt",
